Description: Windows 10 style desktop environment (Wayland)
 Tenwin is a desktop environment for Ubuntu that looks and works like the
 Windows 10 desktop: taskbar with Start menu, live tiles and search, Action
 Center with notifications and quick actions, Alt+Tab and Task View, Aero
 Snap and the familiar Win key shortcuts, desktop icons, a File Explorer with
 ribbon, a Settings app and a lock screen.
 .
 It is built on the labwc Wayland compositor. Light and dark mode and German
 and English translations are included.

Package: tenwin-greeter
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-lightdm-1,
         lightdm,
         python3-gi,
         tenwin-desktop (>= ${source:Version})
Description: Windows 10 style sign-in screen for LightDM
 A LightDM greeter for the Tenwin desktop: lock screen style curtain with
 clock and date, user picture, password field, user list, session and power
 menus.
 .
 Installing this package does not switch the display manager. Select LightDM
 with "sudo dpkg-reconfigure lightdm" or use Tenwin's install.sh.
